<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # What Is Renewable Energy? – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 10px; font-style: italic;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Renewable Energy in Panama</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> What Is Renewable Energy?</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Express opinions about familiar topics. Interactive: Collaborate verbally in small group projects.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can express simple opinions on renewable energy by providing logical reasons and relevant examples (e.g., "I believe solar energy is better because Panama has long hours of sunlight, making it efficient and cost-effective." "I think wind energy is helpful because Penonome has strong, consistent winds, which makes wind turbines effective at generating power.")
            Can collaborate in small groups to choose the best renewable energy option for a specific situation (e.g., "We think wind turbines are good for the countryside in Los Santos because there's a lot of open space and strong winds." "We think hydroelectric power is good for areas near the Chiriqui Viejo River because it can provide consistent energy.")
            Can share a personal view on conserving energy (e.g., "We should all unplug devices when they're not in use to save energy and protect the environment.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying images of various energy sources used in Panama (e.g., solar panels, wind turbines, hydroelectric dams, cars at a gas station). Students are asked to verbally identify them and categorize them as "renewable" or "non-renewable." The teacher then prompts, "Which type of energy source do you think is better for Panama's future? Why?" to initiate opinion sharing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models expressing an opinion and justifying it using target language. For example, "I believe solar energy is better for Panama because we have so much sunlight. It’s a clean and sustainable source." The teacher highlights words like "believe," "because," "clean," "sustainable," and focuses on stress in "renewable" and "sustainable."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of "justify" and "renewable energy."</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'I think solar energy is good,' do I need to explain WHY it's good? (Yes, you need to justify.)"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is wind energy something we can use forever, or will it run out quickly? (Use forever, so it's renewable.)"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher writes key phrases for expressing opinions and justifications on the board (e.g., "I believe...", "I think...", "In my opinion...", "because...", "since...", "as a result of...").</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Renewable Energy in Panama".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio dialogue (or written transcript, read aloud by the teacher) between two Panamanian teenagers, 'Ana' and 'Carlos,' discussing the benefits and challenges of different renewable energy sources for their region in Panama. The dialogue will include opinions, justifications, gerunds, present continuous, and target vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">*Example Dialogue Excerpt:*<br>Ana: "Carlos, what do you think about our town investing more in wind energy? I believe it's a good idea because Penonome has strong, consistent winds, making it efficient for power generation."<br>Carlos: "That's true. Wind energy is a clean source. But I think focusing on solar panels might be better for homes, as a result of Panama having long hours of sunlight. Installing more solar panels is helping us consume less electricity from the grid."<br>Ana: "Good point. Saving energy is important. What about hydropower for areas near bigger rivers? That's providing consistent energy."<br>Carlos: "Hydropower is excellent for continuous electricity, but building new infrastructure can impact the environment. We are discussing the best ways to preserve resources."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students understand and identify spoken opinions and justifications related to renewable energy options in Panama.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the dialogue and answer gist questions verbally in pairs:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What type of energy does Ana recommend for Penonome?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Why does Carlos think solar panels are good for homes?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one challenge Carlos mentions about hydropower?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What ongoing action are they discussing to preserve resources?" (Encourages use of present continuous).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice expressing opinions, justifying them using adverbial clauses, and describing actions with gerunds and the present continuous. Focus on stress in multisyllabic words (e.g., "energy," "renewable," "preservation," "sustainability").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: "Sentence Completion & Justification Match" (Pairs):</b> The teacher provides sentence starters on a worksheet. Students complete the sentences verbally with a partner, selecting the best justification.
                        <br><i>Example:</i> "I think ____ energy is efficient ____." (Options: solar/wind/hydro; because Panama has lots of sun/due to strong winds/since it uses rivers).
                        <br><i>Example 2:</i> "_____ energy is important ____." (Options: Saving/Conserving; because it protects the environment/as a result of limited resources).
                        <br>Students take turns completing sentences and orally justifying their choices to their partner, focusing on the correct use of "because," "since," "as," or "due to."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: "Panama Energy Debate Starters" (Small Groups of 3):</b> Students receive cards with specific Panamanian locations (e.g., "a rural village in Chiriqui," "a coastal town in Azuero," "a new apartment building in Panama City") and energy sources. In groups, they take turns expressing opinions and justifying them for a given card.
                        <br><i>Student A:</i> "I believe wind energy is good for Los Santos because there's a lot of open space and strong winds." (Focus on stress in "renewable," "sustainable.")
                        <br><i>Student B:</i> "I disagree. I think solar panels are better since they are cost-effective for individual homes. We are currently seeing many people installing them." (Focus on gerunds like "installing").
                        <br><i>Student C:</i> "Both are good. Conserving electricity is key for any region. Why don't we consider a mix?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer Feedback & Pronunciation Check:</b> While practicing, students gently correct each other on sentence structure, vocabulary use, and pronunciation, especially on multisyllabic words and adverbial clauses. The teacher circulates, providing support and noting common errors for whole-class feedback. Students practice minimal pairs with long and short vowels if needed, focusing on words like "pen" (energy generation) and "pain" (energy strain).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-17 minutes</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Renewable Energy in Panama".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: "Panama's Green Energy Consultants" (Small Groups of 4):</b> Students work in groups, acting as "Green Energy Consultants" for the Panamanian government. Each group receives a specific (imaginary) Panamanian community profile (e.g., "A remote island community in Guna Yala," "A growing agricultural area in Herrera," "A high-rise residential zone in Panama City").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group discusses and debates which renewable energy source(s) (solar, wind, hydroelectric, biomass) would be the most suitable for their assigned community.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students must express their opinions clearly, justify their choices using adverbial clauses (e.g., "We believe solar power is best for this island because it has consistent sun exposure and lacks strong winds"), and collaborate verbally to reach a consensus.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They should incorporate target vocabulary (e.g., efficiency, sustainability, cost-effective, preserve resources) and grammar (e.g., "Using solar panels is a great solution," "They are currently implementing pilot projects").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The groups prepare a brief verbal presentation (1-2 minutes) to the class, summarizing their chosen energy solution and the main reasons (justifications) behind it.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Emphasize sociolinguistic aspect: providing solutions and ideas, focusing on justification and analysis. (e.g., "We need to reduce dependence on fossil fuels in this area, increasing solar energy projects. This benefits both the environment and the economy.").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-assessment.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher uses an observation checklist to assess students' speaking during group presentations, focusing on their ability to express and justify opinions and collaborate verbally.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group verbally presents their chosen renewable energy solution for their assigned Panamanian community to the class, clearly stating their opinion and justifying it with relevant reasons and examples.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation and correct stress in multisyllabic words (e.g., "renewable," "sustainability," "environment").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Incorporates at least 5-7 key words related to renewable energy (e.g., solar, wind, efficiency, preservation, grid).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of opinion and justification:</b> Clearly states an opinion and provides logical reasons using adverbial clauses (e.g., "because," "since," "due to").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaborative interaction:</b> Actively participates in group discussion and supports group decisions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar accuracy:</b> Uses gerunds for environmental actions and present continuous for ongoing projects with reasonable accuracy.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new opinion I expressed today about renewable energy was..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I found it easy/difficult to justify my opinion because..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-8 minutes</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new word or phrase I used today to talk about renewable energy?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I improve my speaking when giving reasons for my opinions?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What aspects of expressing and justifying opinions worked well during the speaking activities? Was the group collaboration effective?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What grammatical structures (gerunds, present continuous, adverbial clauses) or vocabulary terms need further reinforcement for accuracy in speaking? What specific pronunciation challenges did students face with multisyllabic words?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for Lesson 4 (Writing Composition) to help students transfer these spoken justifications into written arguments?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 4, students will use the vocabulary and communicative structures practiced today to write descriptive paragraphs about renewable energy solutions in Panama, focusing on clear explanations and justifications.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 minutes</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>